  "ud5.6:18.1": "The Vinaya version of this passage omits “sixteen” (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd5/en/sujato#13.9.5'>Kd 5:13.9.5</a>). | <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sarena abhaṇi</i> (“intoned”) means “recited with tones”, apparently a reference to a chanting style that made use of or echoed the Vedic tonal system (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>svara</i>). It was allowed for mendicants at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd15/en/sujato#3.2.3'>Kd 15:3.2.3</a>; see too <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd22/en/sujato#1.10.4'>Kd 22:1.10.4</a>. Contrast <i lang='pi' translate='no'>gītassara</i> (“singing sound”, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.209/en/sujato'>AN 5.209</a>), which is not allowed as it is a sensuous song (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn21/en/sujato#1.6.2'>DN 21:1.6.2</a>). ",
